  "text_pages": [
    "Living cost｜TU Support – TOHOKU UNIVERSITY International Support Center –\nLiving cost\nCost of Living in Sendai\nApproximate monthly expenses in Sendai are as follows.\nRent\nStudent Dormitory\n: 13,000 yen to 33,900 yen/month\nStaff Housing Rental (Unfurnished)\n: 7,200yen ~ 39,000yen\nInternational House Rental (Furnished)\n: 14,000yen ~ 46,000yen\nPrivate Apartments (Unfurnished) :\nStudio Unit (1DK) : 30,000yen ~ 80,000 yen\n1 Bedroom (1LDK) : 40,000yen ~ 120,000yen\n2 Bedroom (2LDK) : 50,000 yen ~ 200,000yen\n(price greatly differs based on location, accessibility, etc.)\nMonthly Apartment (Furnished)\nStudio Unit (1K / IDK) : 96,000 yen onwards\n1 Bedroom (1LDK) : 200,000 yen onwards\n2 Bedroom (2LDK) : 230,000 yen onwards\nUtilities\nSingle\n12,000 yen\nCouple\n16,000yen\nFamily of 4\n24,000yen\nLandline Phone\n2,000 yen/month + usage fees\nFood & Groceries\nSingle\n60,000 yen\nCouple\n90,000 yen\nFamily of 4\n130,000 yen\n(excluding tax)\nLife in Sendai\nTohoku University is located in Sendai, a city with a population of about 1,000,000 the largest in the Tohoku Region. For a long time, it has been known as a “City of Trees” for its lush greenery, making it well-suited for student life and contemplation. Well removed from the Tokyo metropolitan area, rent and other costs are relatively low. The appropriate cost of living is shown below, and we believe it is a nice place to live.\nEstimated Cost of Living – International Students\nMonthly Expenses : 80,000 yen to 150,000 yen\nMonthly Rent (Excluding utilities) : 40,000 yen to 60,000 yen\nEstimated Cost of Living – Researchers / Faculty Members\nMonthly Expenses\nSingle : 80, 000 yen – 150,000 yen\nCouple : 120,000 – 190,000 yen\nFamily of 4 (excluding school fees) : 174,000 – 240,000\nMonthly Rent (excluding utilities)\nSingle : 30,000 yen – 80,000 yen\nCouple : 40,000 yen – 120,000 yen\nFamily of 4 : 50,000 yen – 200,000 yen\nSNS"
  ],
